  "dom_id": "step-q183466",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ There exists $x\\in C$ such that ${x}^{2}$ is not positive.",
  "worked_solution": "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(x):{x}^{2}\\text{ is positive},\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in C,\\,¬P(x).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∃x\\in C,\\,¬P(x)) & ≡∀x\\in C,\\,¬¬P(x) \\\\  & ≡∀x\\in C,\\,P(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $∀x\\in C,\\,P(x)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **For all** $x\\in C,$ ${x}^{2}$ is positive.",
